#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# euler_e

#% text
# `euler_e(n)` gives the Euler number `E_n`; `euler_e(n, x)` gives the Euler polynomial.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Odd indices give 0; `E_2`, `E_4`, ... alternate in sign: -1, 5, -61, 1385. The values are exact integers from the secant number recurrence of Brent and Harvey.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
euler_e(10)
#% output
#= -50521

#% cell
euler_e(range(0, 8))
#% output
#= [1, 0, -1, 0, 5, 0, -61, 0, 1385]

#% cell
euler_e(2, x)
#% output
#= -x + x^2

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `bernoulli_b`, `bell_b`
